{"from": "claim:ac-21-25-decree-gentiles", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-15-20-decree-abstentions", "note": "Acts 21:25 restates the same four abstentions decided at the Jerusalem council (Acts 15:20); the two narrative statements are related, not independent evidence for each other."}
{"from": "claim:ac-21-39-tarsus-standing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-09-11-saul-of-tarsus", "note": "Acts 21:39 names Paul's home city Tarsus, already claimed from Acts 9:11; the 21:39 detail is the 'citizen of no insignificant city' praise."}
{"from": "claim:ac-21-18-james-elders", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-15-13-james-answers", "note": "The same James, brother of Jesus, presides over the Jerusalem elders in Acts 15:13 and receives Paul in 21:18."}
{"from": "claim:ac-21-10-agabus-from-judea", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-11-28-agabus-prediction", "note": "The same prophet Agabus predicted the famine in Acts 11:28 and binds Paul's belt in 21:11."}
{"from": "claim:ac-21-26-purification-temple", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:numbers-6-3", "note": "Numbers 6 (the nazirite law) prescribes the vow's completion offerings; a biblical cross-reference, not evidence."}
