{"from": "text:josephus-war-2-261-263", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-prophet-rising", "grade": "A", "note": "War 2.261-263: 'there was an Egyptian false prophet' who 'got together thirty thousand men' and led them from the wilderness to the Mount of Olives; Felix attacked with horsemen and footmen, and the Egyptian fled."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-169-172", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-prophet-rising", "grade": "A", "note": "Ant. 20.169-172: an Egyptian false prophet led the multitude 'to the Mount of Olives'; Felix attacked with cavalry, and the Egyptian fled - grade A for the rising (split from claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-4000 per the architect's Acts 21 ruling)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-21-38", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-prophet-rising", "note": "Acts 21:38 records the tribune's question about the Egyptian who stirred up sedition and led four thousand into the wilderness; the rumour claim is claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-4000, the rising as Josephus describes it is this claim."}
